rlm-tfapply [TERRAFORM-APPLY-ARGS...]

Apply the saved plan file written by `rlm-tfplan` (`latest.tfplan` by
default), so what gets applied is exactly what was reviewed rather than
a freshly re-computed plan.

Refuses to run when `terraform` is not on `$PATH`, or when the plan file
does not exist in the current directory — the latter turns the usual
"wrong directory" and "forgot to plan" mistakes into a clear message.

Terraform will happily apply a saved plan even after the `.tf` sources
have been edited, silently leaving those edits out of the run, so any
`*.tf` / `*.tf.json` file newer than the plan file is reported as a
warning on stderr. The warning does not block the apply; re-run
`tfplan` to fold the edits in.

Any extra arguments are passed to `terraform apply` ahead of the plan
file, so flags like `-parallelism=` and `-lock-timeout=` work as usual.
Flags that terraform rejects when applying a saved plan (`-var`,
`-target`, `-refresh`, …) belong on `tfplan` instead. The function's
exit status is terraform's.

This is the function form of the older `ta` alias, which remains
available.

ARGUMENTS
  TERRAFORM-APPLY-ARGS   Optional; forwarded verbatim to
                         `terraform apply`, before the plan file.

ENVIRONMENT
  TFPLAN_FILE   Plan file to apply (optional, default
                `latest.tfplan`). Shared with `rlm-tfplan`, so setting
                it for both keeps the pair in sync.

REQUIRES
  terraform
